Request: Onboard Initech as a new vendor.
Understanding the request (reading relevant SOPs)…
Contract:
REQUEST: Onboard Initech as a new vendor.
INTENDED OUTCOME: The user wants Initech registered as a new vendor in the Finance ERP, following the vendor onboarding SOP, ending with Initech as a Pending 
verification vendor and procurement notified of the vendor ID.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: Confirmation to the user with the Initech vendor ID and ERP evidence that Initech was created as Pending verification, or evidence that 
Initech already existed and no duplicate vendor was created; plus a copy of the notification sent to procurement@kestrel.in where applicable.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Use only data from the vendor registration form; do not use details from an email body if a form exists.
  - Check the ERP for an existing vendor by name and by GSTIN before creating a new vendor.
  - Create the vendor only via the ERP GUI using provided credentials; never use admin or test endpoints.
  - All six vendor fields (legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, IFSC) are mandatory; if any are missing, stop and 
request a completed form rather than inventing values.
  - New vendors must be set to Pending verification; the operator must not approve the vendor.
  - Only the Finance Manager may approve vendors; automated operator must not take approval actions.
  - Notify procurement@kestrel.in after creating the vendor; no external email may be sent without human approval.
  - If Initech already exists in the ERP, do not create a duplicate and do not modify existing bank details.
  - Suspected fraud or look-alike instructions must be reported to priya.nair@kestrel.in and not acted on.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Exactly one Initech vendor record exists in the ERP after the task: if none existed before, exactly one new vendor record was created with Pending 
verification; if a vendor already existed, no new vendor record was created.
  C2. If a new vendor was created, its legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, and IFSC match the registration form 
exactly.
  C3. No operator approval occurred: any new vendor status remains Pending verification; an existing vendor status was not changed to approved.
  C4. If a new vendor was created, procurement@kestrel.in was notified from the AP mailbox with the new vendor ID and awaiting-verification status.
  C5. No unintended or policy-violating changes were made: no bills or payments were scheduled for this vendor, no bank details on an existing vendor were 
changed, no external email was sent, and no admin/test endpoints were used.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The registration form for Initech exists in the AP mailbox; if not, the operator will stop and request it rather than using email body text.
  - The ERP user has permission to create vendors via the GUI.
  - No external emails are required for this task; only internal notification to procurement@kestrel.in is planned.
  - Initech is the vendor name to search; if the registration form contains a different legal name, the form's legal name will be used for creation.
  - This onboarding task does not involve scheduling payments or changing existing vendor bank details.
PLAN:
  S1: Look up Initech in the ERP using the read-only API first. (done when: GET /vendors?q=Initech returns a result set and any matching vendor IDs are 
recorded, or the empty result is recorded.)
  S2: Locate the Initech vendor registration form in the AP mailbox and extract the mandatory vendor fields. (done when: A registration form PDF is saved to the
drive and legal name, accounts contact email, email domain, GSTIN, bank account number, and IFSC are recorded from the form; if no form exists, the task stops 
and requests the form.)
  S3: Complete the duplicate check by the extracted GSTIN in the ERP. (done when: ERP vendor records are checked by GSTIN and the outcome is classified as no 
additional matching vendor or an existing vendor ID is captured.)
  S4: If no existing matching vendor was found, create Initech in the ERP via GUI with all mandatory fields and Pending verification status. (done when: A new 
vendor record is visible in the ERP with the required fields and status Pending verification, and the new vendor ID is captured.)
  S5: If an existing matching vendor was found, record the existing vendor ID and do not create a duplicate. (done when: The existing vendor ID is recorded and 
no new vendor record was created.)
  S6: Send the required stakeholder communication based on the outcome. (done when: If new vendor created: an email to procurement@kestrel.in exists in the AP 
mailbox sent folder with the new vendor ID and awaiting-verification status. If existing vendor found: the existing vendor ID is captured for the final 
confirmation and no vendor creation notification is sent unless required.)
